course: dictionary
lesson: 3616
title: Words for people and their jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word ending in -maker often tells you what someone makes. A baker makes bread, and a filmmaker makes films. Look at the word parts: film plus maker.
explain: «Wildlife filmmakers wait quietly in hides for weeks or months.» The clue is in the words around it: they film animals in nature. A hide is a hidden place where you can watch wild animals without them seeing you.
explain: «For Titanic in 1997, the filmmakers built a large part of the ship.» Filmmakers do more than hold cameras. They plan, build and decide how a film looks. Some are young filmmakers who make short films on a phone.
fact: A filmmaker is a person who makes films.
fact: A filmmaker is often a director or producer, the person with the main ideas for a film.
fact: «Filmmakers» is the plural, meaning more than one filmmaker.
fact: «Award-winning filmmaker» means a filmmaker who has won a prize for their work.
fact: Wildlife filmmakers can use hidden cameras, drones and night cameras so they do not disturb animals.
exercise: What is a filmmaker? | *A person who makes films | A machine that plays films | A film star who only acts | A person who sells cinema tickets
exercise: In «Wildlife filmmakers wait quietly in hides», which word tells you the filmmakers work with animals in nature? | weeks | *wildlife | months | hides
exercise: The Titanic filmmakers did not sink a real ship. What did they use instead? | *Models, water tanks and computer effects | Only drawings on paper | A giant swimming pool with a boat | A real ship from the harbour
test: In «an award-winning filmmaker», what does award-winning mean? | Someone who has finished making a film | *Someone who has won a prize for their work | Someone who wins races | Someone who has never seen a film
test: Which word means a person who makes films? | Filmgoer | *Filmmaker | Filmstrip | Filmset
exam: Ruby makes short films on her phone and plans every shot. Which word best describes her? | Cinema usher | *Young filmmaker | Film critic | Ticket seller
